  "title": "A route criterion decides which gluing lines an opened handle reaches",
  "subject": "Which three-point crossing knots are new at a plane gluing line near an opened handle",
  "conclusion": "A three-point crossing knot at a gluing line is generated when one of the line's points separates it or a pair of the line's points, forced by the near pair and covered by the far point's excluded block, carries a two-step elimination. With a Fano handle attached at a point of plane pieces and opened by the removal, the new knots are exactly the candidates without such a route, so creation depends on the plane piece only through its transfer.",
